WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.400
Welcome to Fundamentals of Computer Programming at Ain Shams University, Faculty of Engineering.

2
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:14.200
In this course, all assignments, C++ starter code, and automated grading run on GitHub through Classroom 50.

3
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:22.267
Step 1: Before opening any assignment link, accept your invitation to join the asu-cse GitHub Organization.

4
00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:30.400
Check your email or visit github.com/asu-cse and click Accept Invitation to join the classroom student team.

5
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:38.400
Step 2: Open the assignment acceptance link shared by your instructor on classroom50.org and click Accept assignment.

6
00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:45.667
Classroom 50 automatically creates your private repository with starter code and opens your Feedback Pull Request.

7
00:00:45.667 --> 00:00:55.200
Step 3: Clone your personal repository, edit hello.cpp to print Hello, world!, and test it locally with g++.

8
00:00:55.200 --> 00:01:03.200
Commit and push your code to submit. Never edit or delete .classroom50.yaml or the autograde workflow file.

9
00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:11.800
Step 4: Every push is graded automatically. Open GitHub Releases in your repository to view your test score out of 3.

10
00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:19.600
Check Pull Request #1 ('Feedback') for inline comments from your instructor and TAs. Never close or merge it.

11
00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:27.733
Remember the four Golden Rules: never touch system files, only edit allowed files, and always clone your personal repo.

12
00:01:27.733 --> 00:01:35.067
Use the official asu-cse links on screen to get started. Best of luck with your programming coursework!
